  "data_summary": "Dataset: 13258 rows x 6 columns. Target column: 'global_sales'.\nInferred task type: regression.\n\nColumns:\n  - Name: dtype=object, missing=0.0%, cardinality=9691, examples='Super Mario Bros.', 'Mario Kart Wii', 'Pokemon Red/Pokemon Blue', 'Tetris', 'New Super Mario Bros.'\n  - Platform: dtype=object, missing=0.0%, cardinality=31, examples='NES', 'Wii', 'GB', 'DS', 'PS3'\n  - Year: dtype=int64, missing=0.0%, cardinality=38, min=1980 max=2017 mean=2006\n  - Genre: dtype=object, missing=0.0%, cardinality=12, examples='Platform', 'Racing', 'Role-Playing', 'Puzzle', 'Misc'\n  - Publisher: dtype=object, missing=0.4%, cardinality=546, examples='Nintendo', 'Take-Two Interactive', 'Sony Computer Entertainment', 'Activision', 'Microsoft Game Studios'\n  - global_sales (TARGET): dtype=float64, missing=0.0%, cardinality=566, min=0.01 max=40.24 mean=0.5298\n\nFirst 5 rows:\n                    Name Platform  Year        Genre Publisher  global_sales\n       Super Mario Bros.      NES  1985     Platform  Nintendo         40.24\n          Mario Kart Wii      Wii  2008       Racing  Nintendo         35.82\nPokemon Red/Pokemon Blue       GB  1996 Role-Playing  Nintendo         31.37\n                  Tetris       GB  1989       Puzzle  Nintendo         30.26\n   New Super Mario Bros.       DS  2006     Platform  Nintendo         30.01",
  "analysis": "\n\n# Task & Target Analysis\n- **Task Type:** Regression.\n- **Target Column:** `global_sales`.\n- **Target Distribution:** Highly right-skewed (mean=0.53, max=40.24). Most games sell <1M copies, while blockbusters reach 40M. This skew necessitates searching target transformations (e.g., `Log1p`, `Yeo-Johnson`) to stabilize variance and improve model convergence. Class balance is N/A (regression), but outlier handling or robust loss functions (e.g., Huber) should be considered.\n\n# Column Profile & Cardinality\n- **High-Cardinality Text/Categorical:**\n  - `Name` (cardinality=9691, ~73% unique): Effectively unique identifiers. Risk of overfitting/leakage if not handled carefully. Treat as free-text or consider dropping if generalization to unseen games is required.\n  - `Publisher` (cardinality=546, missing=0.4%): Medium-high cardinality. Requires embedding or target-based encoding.\n- **Low-Cardinality Categorical:**\n  - `Platform` (cardinality=31): Console generation/type.\n  - `Genre` (cardinality=12): Game category.\n- **Numeric/Temporal:**\n  - `Year` (cardinality=38, range 1980-2017): Acts as temporal trend. Could be numeric (linear trend) or binned (eras/generations).\n\n# Preprocessing & Encoding Options\n- **High-Cardinality Encoders:** For `Name` and `Publisher`, search between `MinHashEncoder` (fast, robust) and `GapEncoder` (captures semantic topics). For `Publisher`, `TargetEncoder` (with cross-validation) is also a strong candidate.\n- **Low-Cardinality Encoders:** `OneHotEncoder` (sparse) vs `OrdinalEncoder` (for tree models).\n- **Missing Values:** `Publisher` has 0.4% missing; use simple imputation (\"Unknown\") or let the encoder handle it.\n- **Scaling:** Tree-based models do not require scaling; linear models will need `StandardScaler` on encoded outputs.\n- **Candidate Model Families:**\n  1.  **Gradient Boosting:** `HistGradientBoostingRegressor`, `XGBoost`, or `LightGBM` (handle categorical encodings well, robust to skew).\n  2.  **Linear Baseline:** `Ridge` (with hashed/text encodings).\n  3.  **Random Forest:** `RandomForestRegressor` (good baseline for tabular data).\n\n# Specific Column Operators\n- **`Name` (Text):** Requires a dedicated text encoder (`MinHashEncoder` or `GapEncoder`). *Search Option:* Include vs. Exclude this column (including it may cause leakage if the test set contains known titles).\n- **`Year` (Temporal):** Search treating as **numeric** (continuous trend) vs. **categorical** (specific year effects) vs. **binned** (e.g., 80s, 90s, 2000s, 2010s).\n- **`global_sales` (Target):** Apply `TargetTransformer` (e.g., `Log1p`) before fitting, inverse transform for predictions.\n\n# Relational & Auxiliary Opportunities\n- **Auxiliary Tables:** None listed in the dataset summary.\n- **Join Keys:** N/A.\n- **Aggregations:** N/A. (If external data were available, aggregating historical sales by `Publisher` or `Platform` would be highly predictive).",
  "spec_raw": "\n\n{\n  \"cleaner\": {\"params\": {\"drop_if_constant\": {\"choice\": [false, true]}}},\n  \"vectorizer\": {\n    \"slots\": {\n      \"high_cardinality\": [\"skrub.GapEncoder\", \"skrub.MinHashEncoder\"],\n      \"low_cardinality\": [\"sklearn.preprocessing.OneHotEncoder\", \"sklearn.preprocessing.OrdinalEncoder\"],\n      \"numeric\": [\"passthrough\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"scoped_encodings\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"name_encoding\",\n      \"cols\": [\"Name\"],\n      \"options\": [\"skrub.MinHashEncoder\", \"skrub.GapEncoder\", \"skip\"],\n      \"position\": \"pre_encode\",\n      \"additive\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stages\": [\n    {\"name\": \"scale\", \"options\": [\"skip\", \"sklearn.preprocessing.StandardScaler\"]},\n    {\"name\": \"feature_eng\", \"options\": [\"skip\", {\"name\": \"sklearn.preprocessing.PolynomialFeatures\", \"params\": {\"degree\": {\"int\": [2, 3]}}}]}\n  ],\n  \"model\": [\n    {\"name\": \"sklearn.ensemble.HistGradientBoostingRegressor\", \"prior\": 0.8, \"params\": {\n      \"learning_rate\": {\"float\": [0.01, 0.3], \"log\": true},\n      \"max_iter\": {\"int\": [100, 600]},\n      \"max_depth\": {\"int\": [2, 16]},\n      \"l2_regularization\": {\"float\": [0.0, 1.0]}\n    }},\n    {\"name\": \"lightgbm.LGBMRegressor\", \"prior\": 0.7, \"params\": {\n      \"n_estimators\": {\"int\": [100, 500]},\n      \"learning_rate\": {\"float\": [0.01, 0.3], \"log\": true},\n      \"num_leaves\": {\"int\": [15, 127]},\n      \"max_depth\": {\"int\": [3, 16]},\n      \"colsample_bytree\": {\"float\": [0.5, 1.0]},\n      \"reg_lambda\": {\"float\": [0.0, 5.0]}\n    }},\n    {\"name\": \"sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestRegressor\", \"params\": {\n      \"n_estimators\": {\"int\": [100, 500]},\n      \"max_depth\": {\"int\": [3, 30]},\n      \"min_samples_leaf\": {\"int\": [1, 10]},\n      \"max_features\": {\"choice\": [\"sqrt\", \"log2\", 1.0]}\n    }},\n    {\"name\": \"sklearn.linear_model.Ridge\", \"params\": {\n      \"alpha